{"study_accession":"PRJNA412227","secondary_study_accession":"SRP118909","title":"Epigenomes and Transcriptomes of human monocytes from Hyper IgD Syndrome (HIDS) patients","description":"Innate immune memory, also refered to as trained immunity (TRIM) is the phenomenon whereby innate immune cells such as monocytes or macrophages undergo functional reprogramming after exposure to microbial components. In this study we performed epigenomic and transcriptomic analysis of HIDS (Hyper IgD Syndrome) patients at baseline, and after 24 hours culture in media (RPMI only) or media + 10ng/mL LPS. HIDS is associated with the accumulation of mevalonate, a monocyte trainer. Overall design: HIDS patients were recruited and monocytes were isolated for ChIP-seq and RNA-seq.","pubmed":"29328908","geo_series":"","n_samples":18,"study_labels":[],"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN07702755","study_accession":"PRJNA412227","blood_class":"blood_cells","class_from":"sample","title":"HIDS_Patient3_LPS_d1_RNAseq","description":"HIDS_Patient3_LPS_d1_RNAseq","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM2794004","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2018-01-09","attributes":[["source_name","HIDS monocyte cultured in media (RPMI) with 10ng/mL LPS for 24 hours"],["cell_type","Monocyte"],["treatment","cultured in media (RPMI) with 10ng/mL LPS for 24 hours"],["disease","Hyper IgD Syndrome (HIDS)"],["tissue","Adult Peripheral Blood"],["donor","HIDS_patient_3"],["chip antibody","missing"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR6077582","experiment_accession":"SRX3217237","library_layout":"SINGLE","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina HiSeq 2000","read_count":26178634,"base_count":1099502628,"first_public":"2018-01-09","experiment_title":"Illumina HiSeq 2000 sequencing: GSM2794004: HIDS_Patient3_LPS_d1_RNAseq Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"labels":[],"single_cell":false},{"sample_accession":"SAMN07702756","study_accession":"PRJNA412227","blood_class":"blood_cells","class_from":"sample","title":"HIDS_